{
  "Name": "Adobe Flash Player ByteArray With Workers Use After Free",
  "Description": "This module exploits a use-after-free vulnerability in Adobe Flash Player. The vulnerability occurs when the ByteArray assigned to the current ApplicationDomain is freed from an ActionScript worker, which can fill the memory and notify the main thread to corrupt the new contents. This module has been tested successfully on Windows 7 SP1 (32-bit), IE 8 to IE 11 and Flash 16.0.0.296.",
